@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 Alarm 创建、去重、传播与异步通知

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #111827
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #111827
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActorBorderColor #111827
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #111827
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam QueueBorderColor #111827
skinparam QueueBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam NoteBorderColor #92400E
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #374151
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F9FAFB
skinparam BoxBorderColor #4B5563
skinparam BoxBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

actor "REST Client" as Client
box "Application / REST" #EFF6FF
participant "AlarmController" as Controller
participant "DefaultTbAlarmService" as App
participant "EntityActionService" as Action
end box

box "Alarm Application Service" #ECFDF5
participant "DefaultAlarmSubscriptionService" as Subscription
participant "NotificationRuleProcessor" as Notification
participant "SubscriptionManagerService" as WS
end box

box "DAO" #F8FAFC
participant "BaseAlarmService" as Service
participant "JpaAlarmDao" as Dao
participant "AlarmRepository" as Repository
participant "EntityAlarmRepository" as EntityAlarmRepo
end box

database "PostgreSQL\nalarm / alarm_types / entity_alarm" as PG
queue "Rule Engine Queue" as Queue
participant "RuleNodeActor" as Actor
participant "TbCreateAlarmNode" as Node
participant "TbDeviceProfileNode\nAlarmState" as Profile

== REST create-or-update ==
Client -> Controller: POST /api/alarm\nAlarm JSON
activate Controller
Controller -> Controller: set current tenant\ncheck Alarm and originator permissions
Controller -> App: save(alarm, currentUser)
activate App
App -> App: actionType = id == null ? ADDED : UPDATED
App -> Subscription: createAlarm(request)
activate Subscription
Subscription -> Subscription: read API usage state
Subscription -> Service: createAlarm(request, creationEnabled)
activate Service
Service -> Service: validate fields and timestamps\nrecompute customer from originator
Service -> Dao: createOrUpdateActiveAlarm(request, enabled)
activate Dao
Dao -> Dao: choose edgeAlarmId or random UUID\nserialize details and propagation types
Dao -> Repository: createOrUpdateActiveAlarm(flat parameters)
activate Repository
Repository -> PG: SELECT create_or_update_active_alarm(...)
activate PG
PG -> PG: SELECT active by originator_id + type\nAND cleared=false ORDER BY start_ts DESC FOR UPDATE

alt active row does not exist and creation enabled
  PG -> PG: INSERT alarm\nacknowledged=false, cleared=false
  PG -> PG: INSERT alarm_types\nON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
  PG -> PG: SELECT alarm_info
  PG --> Repository: JSON created=true, modified=true
else active row exists and fields changed
  PG -> PG: UPDATE same alarm id\nseverity/time/details/propagation
  PG -> PG: SELECT alarm_info
  PG --> Repository: JSON modified=true + old
else active row exists and fields are identical
  PG --> Repository: JSON modified=false
else no active row and creation disabled
  PG --> Repository: JSON success=false
end
deactivate PG
Repository --> Dao: JSON text
deactivate Repository
Dao -> Dao: parse AlarmApiCallResult
Dao --> Service: result
deactivate Dao

alt result contains Alarm
  Service -> Service: publish SaveEntityEvent\nevict alarm-type cache
  Service -> Service: calculate propagation entities
  loop originator + parents + owner + tenant
    Service -> EntityAlarmRepo: save(EntityAlarm)
    EntityAlarmRepo -> PG: INSERT or UPDATE entity_alarm
    alt one propagation row fails
      EntityAlarmRepo --> Service: exception
      Service -> Service: log warning and continue
    end
  end
end
Service --> Subscription: result + propagated entities
deactivate Service

alt successful and modified
  Subscription -> WS: submit async onAlarmUpdate per entity
  Subscription -> Notification: submit async AlarmTrigger
  opt severity changed
    Subscription -> PG: save SYSTEM alarm_comment
  end
end
Subscription --> App: synchronous result
deactivate Subscription

alt result modified
  App -> Action: logEntityAction(ADDED or UPDATED)
  activate Action
  Action -> Notification: EntitiesLimitTrigger for ADDED\nand EntityActionTrigger for ADDED or UPDATED
  Action -> Queue: push ENTITY_CREATED or ENTITY_UPDATED
  Action -> PG: async save audit_log
  Action --> App: returns without waiting for consumers/audit
  deactivate Action
end
App --> Controller: Alarm
deactivate App
Controller --> Client: HTTP response
deactivate Controller

note over PG
Alarm function and later entity_alarm saves do not share
one explicit service transaction in this creation path.
WebSocket, notification, Queue and audit are also outside it.
end note

== Explicit Create Alarm Rule Node ==
Queue -> Actor: input TbMsg
activate Actor
Actor -> Node: onMsg(ctx, msg)
activate Node
Node -> Subscription: findLatestActiveByOriginatorAndType(...)
Subscription -> Service: findLatestActiveByOriginatorAndType(...)
Service -> PG: SELECT latest active
PG --> Service: Alarm or null
Service --> Subscription: Alarm or null
Subscription --> Node: Alarm or null
Node -> Node: build details asynchronously\nbuild new Alarm or mutate existing
Node -> Subscription: createAlarm(request) or updateAlarm(request)
Subscription -> Service: same persistence path
Service --> Subscription: AlarmApiCallResult
Subscription --> Node: result
Node -> Queue: enqueue alarmActionMsg\nENTITY_CREATED or ENTITY_UPDATED
alt producer success
  Queue --> Node: onSuccess
  Node -> Actor: tellNext(ALARM, Created or Updated)
else producer failure
  Queue --> Node: onFailure
  Node -> Actor: tellFailure(ALARM)
end
Node --> Actor: callback path completes
deactivate Node
deactivate Actor

note over Node,PG
The Alarm is already persisted before alarmActionMsg enqueue.
Queue failure cannot roll it back.
end note

== Device Profile Alarm Rule ==
Queue -> Actor: telemetry or attributes TbMsg
activate Actor
Actor -> Profile: onMsg(ctx, msg)
activate Profile
Profile -> Profile: load DeviceState and latest snapshot\nmerge update, evaluate severity rules
alt new matching alarm
  Profile -> Subscription: createAlarm(request)
else existing alarm and allowed severity
  Profile -> Subscription: updateAlarm(request)
else no create rule and clear rule matches
  Profile -> Subscription: clearAlarm(...)
end
Subscription -> Service: same persistence path
alt snapshot, evaluation and Alarm service succeed
  Service --> Subscription: AlarmApiCallResult
  Subscription --> Profile: result
  Profile -> Queue: enqueueForTellNext(ALARM relation msg)
  Profile -> Actor: tellSuccess(original telemetry/attribute msg)
else synchronous exception
  Service --> Subscription: exception
  Subscription --> Profile: exception propagates
  Profile -> Actor: onMsg throws; no tellSuccess
end
deactivate Profile
deactivate Actor

note over Profile,Queue
On the successful path, original message success is independent
from the extra Alarm message producer callback.
The profile path does not call REST audit/EntityAction orchestration.
end note

== Concurrent first-create window ==
participant "Request A" as A
participant "Request B" as B
A -> PG: SELECT active FOR UPDATE
PG --> A: no row, therefore no tuple lock
B -> PG: SELECT active FOR UPDATE
PG --> B: no row, therefore no tuple lock
A -> PG: INSERT alarm id A
PG --> A: success
B -> PG: INSERT alarm id B
PG --> B: success possible
note over A,B
The partial active index is not UNIQUE.
Two active alarms may be inserted for the same originator and type.
end note

@enduml
